<title>CHINA: Agri Bank of China seen mandating $120 mln FRCD.</title>
<headline>Agri Bank of China seen mandating $120 mln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agricultural Bank of China, acting through its Singapore branch, will launch a US$120 million floating rate certificates of deposit issue soon, bankers said.</p>
<p>They said Societe Generale Asia and Bayerische Landesbank are close to receiving a mandate to arrange the deal.</p>
<p>The certificates will carry a maturity of five years and the all-in return for top-tier managers is expected to be in low 30s basis points over the London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>Agricultural Bank of China is rated Baa1 by Moody's Investors Service.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
